texts={
'S01':'Product defines the adopted intended product and end state, including capabilities still to be built; Goals hold current epics or work-wave focus. Requirements own invariant WHAT; accepted design owns structural HOW, interfaces, topology, carriers, file placement and delivery mechanisms; code realises those decisions. Requirements plus accepted design govern implementation, not implementation precedent. Technology choice belongs to design unless already constitutionally constrained.',
'O01':'Under adopted ODD, preserve typed asset boundaries and named published graph functions or compositions as the operative constructive carriers. Declare inputs/outputs, intent, public/helper role, outer/inner vector and refinement relations and produced/consumed asset contracts. Design the typed outcome traversal and its graph-language/runtime carrier before minimal adapters. Local scripts, services, nested calls and packaging cannot acquire rival semantic or graph authority. Public carriers and views reconcile structurally and semantically to their declared authoritative sources; missing, stale or materially conflicting sources leave the affected claim unestablished.',
'O02':'The declared runtime owns continuation and re-entry for its traversal. A bounded domain step returns outputs/results through its published contract; another Product, plugin, service or projection gains no traversal control by invocation or status reporting. Before activation and closure, changes to traversal control, delegation (including worker transport/process supervision), admission, evidence evaluation, closure, assurance, retry or continuation require an authority audit of actual call paths and outputs, each operation owner and grant, and absence of a rival controller. Missing or conflicting authority prevents affected activation and closure. Product owns concrete audit inventory and implementation protocol; ODD mandates no process API, event/replay seam or fixed five-surface design.',
'O03':'Keep runtime control, evidence evaluation, operation grants and acceptance separately bound to their declared contracts and owners. F_P/F_H specialisations confer no additional authority. The Product owns evaluator decomposition, selection algorithm, storage and recovery protocol; ODD requires no four-function evaluator API or fixed constructive loop. An implementation refactor must preserve the actual adopted Product contracts as well as these method boundaries.',
'O04':'The selected outcome comes from SPEC_METHOD, never traversal activity, a model, gap or projection. Each invoked step binds graph contract, inputs, target, obligations, grant and lawful stop conditions. Changed commitments re-enter their owning surface; re-entry requests do not select replacement outcomes or grant effects. Work remains within the admitted outcome or bounded basis and stops under its governing terminal/exhaustion conditions. Missing lawful graph authority is not repaired by an unpublished fallback or local controller.',
'O05':'Tracking and reconciliation are required: keep current obligations, decisions, progress and unresolved matters available to later actors and reconcile with the authoritative mutable workspace before material reliance. An optional generic register or functionally equivalent LLM/other mechanism may do this. Declared sources and evidence can be re-acquired by reference; record needed transient observations, judgments, residuals and authority decisions that later steps cannot otherwise acquire. Preserve subject, basis, scope, evidence and authority plus enough prior/current identity for corrections. No mandatory immutable ledger, ledger-only attention, every-callout capture or event-log admission is imposed. Product-specific evidence/storage duties still apply. An F_P worker must not receive an F_D-authored semantic extraction recipe when its edge requires F_P judgment.',
'O06':'An artifact, worker report or successful process exit alone cannot close a traversal or accept a Product. Evaluation, artifact admission and acceptance retain their declared contracts and owners. Each evaluation names its predicate and core result; evidence for one predicate cannot satisfy another. Runtime-specific disposition names/refinements belong to the Product and require declared mappings. ODD defines no closure-decision enum or ledger fold. Missing coverage and material residuals remain visible; traversal closure does not imply construction availability, Product acceptance or RELEASE successor disposition.',
'O07':'Lawful continuation and re-entry follow the declared graph and runtime ownership. Material surprise or changed basis re-enters ACTIVATION feedback/diagnosis rules. Resumption acquires relevant current sources and needed prior step-produced facts; bounded return does not erase progress or obligations. Activity, timeout or process state alone cannot decide a semantic predicate without its required evidence. The Product supplies any selection algorithm, runtime result vocabulary and recovery protocol; no evaluate_next totality, fixed resume variants, priority fallback or replay-visible yield carrier is mandated by ODD.',
'O08':'A projection names source, subject, scope and validity; it supplies no competing authority. Current asset views reconcile to workspace evidence; execution-history views name supporting records for historical claims. Matching names/output does not prove structural or semantic identity. Missing, stale or conflicting material sources invalidate affected reliance until reconciled; negative projection proof includes structural drift. Preserve needed facts and interpretable provenance, but no universal replay or prescribed causal-carrier chain is required. Published inner steps retain the outer contract and applicable ownership/evidence duties; opaque realization gains no hidden traversal control. Valid unchanged evidence retains only its exact applicable scope.',
'U04':None,
'W11':'Choose the first actually changed layer: goal_reprice for current epics/work-wave focus re-enters Goals; intent_reprice for direction/scope re-enters Intent; product_reprice for the adopted Product definition or intended end state re-enters Product; requirement_reprice for constitutional truth re-enters Requirements; design_reframe for realization structure re-enters Design; realization_refactor for local realization change re-enters only that surface and must prove no upstream drift. A smaller change re-enters below Goals only with an explicit no-upstream-change assertion. A declared change class is never a result: realization_refactor cannot stand in for a satisfied result that no upstream drift occurred. Product may include capabilities still to be built. Derive affected downstream work and evidence. A supported implementation defect under sufficient law is repaired within its grant; changed outcome, scope or territory re-enters its owner before effects.'}
def whole(path,heading):
 lines=(root/path).read_text().splitlines(True);start=next(i for i,x in enumerate(lines) if x.rstrip()==heading);level=len(heading.split(' ')[0]);end=next((i for i in range(start+1,len(lines)) if re.match(r'^#{1,'+str(level)+r'} ',lines[i])),len(lines));return {'source_id':path,'start_line':start+1,'end_line':end}
def translate(path,ref):
 old=subprocess.check_output(['git','show','2c95df2fe4656f1bbe6c4eb2d9f4be6e28446e0d:specification_methodology/v3/build_tenants/common/'+path]).decode().splitlines(True);new=(root/path).read_text().splitlines(True);a,b=ref['start_line']-1,ref['end_line'];mapped=[]
 for tag,i,j,k,l in difflib.SequenceMatcher(a=old,b=new,autojunk=False).get_opcodes():
  if i<b and j>a:
   if tag=='equal':mapped.append((k+max(a-i,0),k+min(b-i,j-i)))
   else:mapped.append((k,l))
 assert mapped
 lo=min(x[0] for x in mapped);hi=max(x[1] for x in mapped);assert hi>lo
 return {'source_id':ref['source_id'],'start_line':lo+1,'end_line':hi}
